./iterations/iter_009/solver_attempt.md:74:   Thresholds \(c_j\le\delta_*\) are nonbinding. The dual hard law is a truncated equal-revenue law on the suffix above \(\delta_*\).
./iterations/iter_009/solver_attempt.md:77:   For \(c_i=r^{m-i}\), \(r=(m-1)/m\), one gets \(\delta_*=r^m=((m-1)/m)^m\), and the primal distribution is uniform over quotes just below the \(c_i\)’s.
